# fixtures/hex/chain/lazy-tail/log.1.hex: store D ([F05 §5.3], [60 §2.5] decision (b) as restated, [72 B1]).
# Commit c1's group is durable and ends at durable_lsn D. Then lazy group L1 (valid) and lazy group L2, which a
# non-durable publish covered (committed_lsn = the end of L2) but no flush made durable. An OS crash lost L2's
# last 512-byte sector, which reads as zero: L2's last record and its chain trailer fail, so the group is
# invalid at a boundary in [durable_lsn, committed_lsn). That boundary is the end of the valid log and the end of
# a reader's visible log: a lost lazy tail, never an error. HEAD.hex: durable_lsn = D, committed_lsn = L2's end.

